.TH VIGILANCE 1 "" "vigilance" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vigilance \- lock / screen-power / idle suite for a Wayland session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smart-lock
.RB [ lock | unlock ]
.br
.B smart-trigger
.RB { lock | listen }
.br
.B panel-power
.RB { off | on }
.br
.B swayidle-mgr ", " osd-mgr ", " idle-capture ", " lock-watch
.SH DESCRIPTION
vigilance is a suite of small, single-purpose tools for what a machine does when
you step away and when you return: lock the screen, blank or power down the
panel, and run your lock/unlock hooks (audio muting, etc.). There is no single
.B vigilance
command; each tool below is invoked by name, or driven by the systemd units in
.IR systemd/ .
.PP
The security-critical paths are swayidle-INDEPENDENT by design. A single idle
daemon that wedges must not be the lock guarantee, so locking is driven through
.B smart-lock
and
.B smart-trigger
from four triggers (idle timer, a manual keybind, suspend, and the logind
Session.Lock signal), each independent of the others.
.SH TOOLS
.TP
.B smart-lock
The lock EXECUTOR: reads a per-display shape, draws a multi-output spanned lock,
runs the lock/unlock hooks. Runs foreground so its unlock wait keeps the locker
alive.
.TP
.B smart-trigger
The robust LAUNCHER / LISTENER: runs the lock on suspend and on the logind
Session.Lock signal, launching swaylock as a separate transient --user unit that
survives the trigger's teardown.
.TP
.B swayidle-mgr
A thin single-instance idle-lock timer (timer-only; the security paths do not
depend on it).
.TP
.B panel-power
Real screen-off over DDC/CI (modeset-safe), plus the peripherals hook. Never
toggles a connector.
.TP
.B osd-mgr
Supervises the on-screen-display server so it self-heals a half-init.
.TP
.B idle-capture ", " lock-watch
Opt-in diagnostics for tracing phantom-relock and idle behaviour.
.SH HOOKS
.B smart-lock
runs every executable in
.IR ~/.config/lock-hooks/lock.d/
on lock and
.IR ~/.config/lock-hooks/unlock.d/
on unlock, passing the event ("lock"/"unlock") as the first argument. This is
the extension point: an integrator drops in its own hooks (audio muting, a
presence beacon, ...); vigilance ships none.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I systemd/smart-trigger.service
The --user Session.Lock listener (install it with
.BR "setup.sh service" ).
.TP
.I systemd/lock-on-sleep.service
The SYSTEM suspend-lock unit (Before=sleep.target); needs root to place under
.IR /etc/systemd/system .
.TP
.I ~/.config/shapes
Optional per-display shape config (swaylock/wallpaper); absent, smart-lock uses
a single-output lock.
.SH RUNTIME DEPENDENCIES
.BR swaylock ", " swayidle ", " wlopm ", " ddcutil .
Optional: a display-shape resolver and a wallpaper slicer for the spanned lock;
each degrades gracefully when absent.
.SH SETUP
.B ./setup.sh install
links the tools (and this page) into
.IR ~/.local ;
.B ./setup.sh service
adds the --user listener;
.B ./setup.sh check
audits the install. See the README.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR swaylock (1),
.BR swayidle (1)
